After 192 pixels: information content 574.6 bits, bits committed 574, finished code 576 bits.
Bits committed minus information content ranges from -1.96 to -0.03.
\image(figures/arithmetic_coding_trace.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Bits committed by the integer encoder (blue) and the information content of the pixels coded so far (red) over the first three images. Grey lines mark the image boundaries.)
\alttext(Two line plots against pixels coded, from 1 to 192. Left: bits committed and information content rise together from 0 to about 575 bits and overlap so closely that they look like one line. Right: their difference stays between about minus 2 and 0 bits throughout, fluctuating from pixel to pixel.)

Each pixel multiplies the width by its probability, so \(-\log_2 w\) climbs by about one
bit for each blank pixel (\(p_0=0.489\)) and by about five bits for each inked one. The
encoder keeps pace. After every pixel the number of bits it has committed is the whole part
of \(-\log_2 w\), or one less. The integer coder does not need the exact real interval,
which is fortunate: by the 14th pixel the width is \(8\times10^{-15}\). Two pixels later
it is only a few times the spacing between doubles near 0.15, and a floating-point coder
would be computing mostly rounding error. After 192 pixels the information content
is 574.6 bits. The encoder has committed 574 bits, and its finished code has 576, within
the two-bit bound. The right panel shows that the committed bits trail the information
content by between 0.03 and 1.96 bits. Those are the bits still held in the 32-bit
register, which the flush writes at the end.

> The pixel distribution, and Huffman's whole bits

How skewed is the source? The table lists each intensity's count and probability, its
ideal code length \(-\log_2 p_s\) and the length \(\ell_s\) of its Huffman codeword from
`dm::algorithms::huffman_code_lengths()`. Huffman's code is the best possible prefix code
with whole-bit lengths. It satisfies the Kraft equality \(\sum_s 2^{-\ell_s}=1\), so it
behaves as if the source had probabilities \(2^{-\ell_s}\). Its excess over the entropy is
the Kullback-Leibler divergence between the real and implied distributions:

$$
\sum_s p_s\ell_s - H=\sum_s p_s\log_2\frac{p_s}{2^{-\ell_s}}=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(p\,\big\|\,2^{-\ell}\right)\ \ge 0 .
$$
\alttext(The sum over s of p s times l s, minus H, equals the sum over s of p s times log base 2 of p s over 2 to the minus l s, which is the Kullback-Leibler divergence from p to 2 to the minus l, and is at least 0.)

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/arithmetic_coding_distribution.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace alg = dm::algorithms;

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto digits = dm::datasets::digits();
  std::vector<int> pixels;
  for (std::size_t r = 0; r < digits.nrows(); ++r)
    for (int i = 0; i < 64; ++i) pixels.push_back(static_cast<int>(digits.double_at(std::format("pixel_{}", i), r)));
  const auto counts = alg::symbol_counts(pixels, 17);
  const auto lengths = alg::huffman_code_lengths(counts);
  const double n = static_cast<double>(pixels.size());

  std::print("| intensity | count | \\(p_s\\) | \\(-\\log_2 p_s\\) | Huffman \\(\\ell_s\\) |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::vector<double> v, p, ideal, huff;
  double expected = 0.0, kraft = 0.0;
  for (int s = 0; s < 17; ++s) {
    const double ps = counts[s] / n;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.4f} | {:.2f} | {} |\n", s, counts[s], ps, -std::log2(ps), lengths[s]);
    v.push_back(s);
    p.push_back(ps);
    ideal.push_back(-std::log2(ps));
    huff.push_back(lengths[s]);
    expected += ps * lengths[s];
    kraft += std::ldexp(1.0, -lengths[s]);
  }
  const double h = alg::shannon_entropy_bits(counts);
  std::print("\nEntropy H = {:.4f} bits; Huffman expected length = {:.4f} bits ({:+.2f}%); "
             "Kraft sum = {}; fixed-length code = {} bits.\n",
             h, expected, 100 * (expected / h - 1), kraft, static_cast<int>(std::ceil(std::log2(17.0))));

  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                 .bars(v, p, "", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 0.8)
                 .title("Pixel intensity distribution")
                 .x_label("intensity")
                 .y_label("probability"));
  layout.add(dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                 .points(v, ideal, "ideal -log2 p", dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 6.0)
                 .points(v, huff, "Huffman length", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 6.0)
                 .legend({"ideal -log2 p", "Huffman length"}, {dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}, dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}})
                 .y_limits(0, 7)
                 .title("Code length per intensity")
                 .x_label("intensity")
                 .y_label("bits"));
  layout.size(1200, 440).save_svg("build/arithmetic_coding_distribution.svg");
}
```
